WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.400
If you have a professional selling plan, you can use the Automate Pricing Tool to adjust

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.640
your prices automatically.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:14.280
This helps your offers remain competitive within the price limits you set.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:19.760
In the Pricing Rules page in Seller Central, you will find two types of predefined pricing

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.920
rules available to you already.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:29.240
These are the Competitive Price Rule by Amazon and the Business Catalog Rule by Amazon.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:34.120
Next to the rule name, you will see columns for the rule type, a short summary of what

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:35.580
the rule does.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:41.160
The marketplaces the rule is active in, the number of SKUs currently enrolled, the status

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:47.520
of the rule, either active, processing, or inactive, and the action column.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:52.200
Carefully read the rule summary for each to determine if it is right for your business.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:57.440
In addition to our predefined pricing rules, you can create a variety of custom rules to

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.300
apply to your catalog by selecting Create Custom Pricing Rule.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:07.240
There are several rule types available to you under the "What type of rule do you want

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.640
to create" drop down.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:15.960
These are Competitive Featured Offer, Competitive Lowest Price, Global Selling Rule, Competitive

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:22.800
External Price, Business Competitive Featured Offer, Business Price and Quantity Discounts,

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.120
and Based on Sales Units.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:30.640
When you select each rule type, a short summary of the rule type will populate.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:35.280
Read each summary carefully to determine which rule type fits your needs.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:39.880
Once you have selected the rule type you want to create, give your rule a short descriptive

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:40.880
name.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:45.440
Next, you will need to select the marketplace or marketplaces you would like your rule to

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:46.440
apply to.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:49.920
You will then be asked to set the parameters for your rule.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:54.120
A series of questions related to the rule you selected will appear.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:58.640
Read each question carefully and fill in the requested information.

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:03.120
If available, hover over the information icon for additional context.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:07.800
You will need to answer all the questions for each marketplace you have selected.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:11.640
Once you have completed the parameters, click Save and Exit.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:17.280
You will see your rule on the Automate Pricing page underneath the predefined pricing rule.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.840
You can repeat this process as many times as you like to create multiple custom pricing

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.000
rules.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:29.140
To learn how to apply pre-populated and custom pricing rules to your SKUs, watch the Automate

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:33.400
Pricing Apply Pricing Rules video in Seller Central.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:39.520
Watch the Automate Pricing change or remove a pricing rule video in Seller University to

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:46.360
learn how to edit a pricing rule pause, resume, delete it, and review your price history.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:50.960
If you're an Amazon business seller, review the Create a Business Pricing Rule Help page

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:56.520
in Seller Central to learn how to automate business price updates based on changes you

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.840
make to your standard consumer prices.
